kwin (4:6.6.6-0ubuntu0.1+moto12) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Wayland backend: cast outputs get no cursor layer, so the cursor is
    rendered into the frame the host shows on the TV.
  * Wayland backend: a cast output takes the lowest free CAST-n name so a
    reconnected TV keeps its output settings.
  * Wayland backend: read host wl_outputs from the raw protocol. KWayland's
    Output::addMode() keeps an iterator across QList::erase and crashed KWin
    whenever the host announced a mode again (phone refresh changes).
  * Input method: KWIN_IM_SHOW_ALWAYS applies to windows on internal outputs
    only; on a cast output the phone is the keyboard.
  * Wayland backend: text the host commits over text-input-v3 (Android
    keyboard: Chinese, emoji) goes to KWin's input method and the focused client.

 -- Moto Linux integration <local@localhost>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0800

kwin (4:6.6.6-0ubuntu0.1+moto11) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Wayland backend: bind the host's wl_output globals. A host output made by
    "Moto" with model "Cast" (the Android host's Miracast display) gets its own
    output (CAST-n, scale MOTO_KWIN_CAST_SCALE, default 1.5) whose window is
    fullscreen on that host output; it is removed with the host output. Phone
    modes, size and Android display settings apply to the primary output only.
    Host wl_output is bound at version 3 so KWayland's release on removal is
    valid (v2 made the host drop the connection).

 -- Moto Linux integration <local@localhost>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:30:00 +0800

